The bridge tests now distinguish every nontrivial primitive on adversarial signs, exercise all three recurrence branches, compare 5,000 inputs against an independently written source-loop oracle, and reject constant, identity, Euclidean-arithmetic, and even-digit mutations. I’m adding a direct supplied-semantics `krun` check for representative source executions as the final operational cross-check.
